      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Climate of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's climate is shaped by latitude, altitude, distance from the sea, and pressure/wind systems.",
        "The South-West Monsoon bifurcates into two main branches: the Arabian Sea branch and the Bay of Bengal branch.",
        "Local winds in India play a vital role in regional weather dynamics preceding the main monsoon.",
        "Global atmospheric-oceanic phenomena like El Niño and La Niña directly influence the strength and variability of the Indian monsoon."
      ],
      "id": "jd8nfg7"
